# PART XII — REQUIRED RESEARCH REPORTS

## 18. Maintain living documentation

Create and continuously update:

**`PROJECT_STATUS.md`**

Current progress, dataset counts, reviewed and provisional status, active work, and known blockers.

**`RESEARCH_GAPS.md`**

Missing capabilities and dataset weaknesses directly connected to Rineya's research.

**`DATASET_QUALITY_REPORT.md`**

Quantitative quality measurements, reviewer feedback, adversarial findings, and unresolved issues.

**`GENERATOR_IMPROVEMENTS.md`**

What changed, why, and whether it fixed the observed problem.

**`CURRICULUM_COVERAGE.md`**

Track and difficulty coverage, independent mechanism counts, and underrepresented reasoning patterns.

**`TRAINING_READINESS.md`**

A future-facing assessment of which datasets are suitable for separate model-training experiments.

This is an assessment of data readiness, not evidence of training effectiveness.

**`GITHUB_BACKUP_LOG.md`**

Every release, commit SHA, remote-verification result, and remaining local-only artifact.

**`NEXT_SESSION_HANDOFF.md`**

The last safe checkpoint, currently approved data versions, unfinished reviews, pending issues, and exact steps required to resume.

Reports must be based on actual files and executable evidence.

