**Identify a research gap → Produce semantic tasks → Compute verified answers → Generate diverse renderings → Obtain independent expert feedback → Perform adversarial attacks → Correct generator weaknesses → Approve examples → Create a versioned release → Push and verify on GitHub.**

## FINAL GOVERNING PRINCIPLE

**One genuinely generalizable, independently verified, carefully constructed example can be more valuable than many repetitive or incorrectly labeled examples.**

Build datasets that encourage Rineya to learn reusable rules, computational procedures, and transferable reasoning skills—not datasets that merely reward memorizing familiar surface patterns.

Protect all existing research evidence.

Prioritize rigorous correctness over volume.

Continuously improve generation quality.

Preserve every approved dataset release through verified GitHub backups.

**Start executing now.**
